{"type":"root","children":[{"type":"heading","depth":1,"id":"writing-styles","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Writing styles"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineComponent","name":"inline-code","tagName":"md-inline-code","attributes":{},"children":[],"properties":{"html":"<span class=\"th-token th-function\">css</span>()","source":"css()"}},{"type":"text","value":" takes style objects and returns a handle. A handle is an opaque value:\nyou pass it to "},{"type":"inlineComponent","name":"inline-code","tagName":"md-inline-code","attributes":{},"children":[],"properties":{"html":"sx","source":"sx"}},{"type":"text","value":", merge it with others, or export it. It is not an object you\ncan read at runtime — by then it is a class string."}]},{"type":"component","name":"code","tagName":"md-code","attributes":{},"children":[],"properties":{"source":"import { css } from \"@kirana-style/core\"\n\nconst panel = css({\n  display: \"grid\",\n  gap: \"0.75rem\",\n  padding: \"1rem\",\n})","lang":"tsx","html":"<span class=\"th-token th-keyword\">import</span> { css } <span class=\"th-token th-keyword\">from</span> <span class=\"th-token th-string\">&quot;@kirana-style/core&quot;</span>\n\n<span class=\"th-token th-keyword\">const</span> panel = <span class=\"th-token th-function\">css</span>({\n  <span class=\"th-token th-property\">display</span>: <span class=\"th-token th-string\">&quot;grid&quot;</span>,\n  <span class=\"th-token th-property\">gap</span>: <span class=\"th-token th-string\">&quot;0.75rem&quot;</span>,\n  <span class=\"th-token th-property\">padding</span>: <span class=\"th-token th-string\">&quot;1rem&quot;</span>,\n})"}},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"property-names","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Property names"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Properties are camelCase: "},{"type":"inlineComponent","name":"inline-code","tagName":"md-inline-code","attributes":{},"children":[],"properties":{"html":"backgroundColor","source":"backgroundColor"}},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"inlineComponent","name":"inline-code","tagName":"md-inline-code","attributes":{},"children":[],"properties":{"html":"paddingInlineStart","source":"paddingInlineStart"}},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"inlineComponent","name":"inline-code","tagName":"md-inline-code","attributes":{},"children":[],"properties":{"html":"gridTemplateColumns","source":"gridTemplateColumns"}},{"type":"text","value":".\nAnything CSS knows about is allowed; anything else is an error\n("},{"type":"inlineComponent","name":"inline-code","tagName":"md-inline-code","attributes":{},"children":[],"properties":{"html":"unknown-property","source":"unknown-property"}},{"type":"text","value":"), so a typo fails the build instead of disappearing."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Custom properties are written as they are in CSS, in quotes:"}]},{"type":"component","name":"code","tagName":"md-code","attributes":{},"children":[],"properties":{"source":"css({\n  \"--card-gap\": \"1rem\",\n  gap: \"var(--card-gap)\",\n})","lang":"tsx","html":"<span class=\"th-token th-function\">css</span>({\n  <span class=\"th-token th-string\">&quot;--card-gap&quot;</span>: <span class=\"th-token th-string\">&quot;1rem&quot;</span>,\n  <span class=\"th-token th-property\">gap</span>: <span class=\"th-token th-string\">&quot;var(--card-gap)&quot;</span>,\n})"}},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"values","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Values"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Values are strings and numbers, exactly as CSS reads them. Kirana does "},{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"not"}]},{"type":"text","value":"\nadd units for you:"}]},{"type":"component","name":"code","tagName":"md-code","attributes":{},"children":[],"properties":{"source":"css({ width: \"5rem\" }) // fine\ncss({ width: 5 }) // error: unitless-length\ncss({ flexGrow: 1 }) // fine - flex-grow takes a number\ncss({ zIndex: 10 }) // fine","lang":"tsx","html":"<span class=\"th-token th-function\">css</span>({ <span class=\"th-token th-property\">width</span>: <span class=\"th-token th-string\">&quot;5rem&quot;</span> }) <span class=\"th-token th-comment\">// fine</span>\n<span class=\"th-token th-function\">css</span>({ <span class=\"th-token th-property\">width</span>: <span class=\"th-token th-number\">5</span> }) <span class=\"th-token th-comment\">// error: unitless-length</span>\n<span class=\"th-token th-function\">css</span>({ <span class=\"th-token th-property\">flexGrow</span>: <span class=\"th-token th-number\">1</span> }) <span class=\"th-token th-comment\">// fine - flex-grow takes a number</span>\n<span class=\"th-token th-function\">css</span>({ <span class=\"th-token th-property\">zIndex</span>: <span class=\"th-token th-number\">10</span> }) <span class=\"th-token th-comment\">// fine</span>"}},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The rule is the CSS rule: a property that takes a "},{"type":"inlineComponent","name":"inline-code","tagName":"md-inline-code","attributes":{},"children":[],"properties":{"html":"&lt;<span class=\"th-token th-tag\">length</span>&gt;","source":"<length>"}},{"type":"text","value":" needs a unit. A\nproperty whose value is a plain number takes a plain number. Guessing "},{"type":"inlineComponent","name":"inline-code","tagName":"md-inline-code","attributes":{},"children":[],"properties":{"html":"px","source":"px"}},{"type":"text","value":" is how\na styling system ends up with values it cannot explain, so the compiler asks you\ninstead."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Invalid values are errors too ("},{"type":"inlineComponent","name":"inline-code","tagName":"md-inline-code","attributes":{},"children":[],"properties":{"html":"invalid-value","source":"invalid-value"}},{"type":"text","value":"), checked against the property's\nreal grammar:"}]},{"type":"component","name":"code","tagName":"md-code","attributes":{},"children":[],"properties":{"source":"css({ display: \"flx\" }) // error: invalid-value\ncss({ margin: \"1px;\" }) // error: invalid-value - a stray semicolon","lang":"tsx","html":"<span class=\"th-token th-function\">css</span>({ <span class=\"th-token th-property\">display</span>: <span class=\"th-token th-string\">&quot;flx&quot;</span> }) <span class=\"th-token th-comment\">// error: invalid-value</span>\n<span class=\"th-token th-function\">css</span>({ <span class=\"th-token th-property\">margin</span>: <span class=\"th-token th-string\">&quot;1px;&quot;</span> }) <span class=\"th-token th-comment\">// error: invalid-value - a stray semicolon</span>"}},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"several-objects-one-handle","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Several objects, one handle"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineComponent","name":"inline-code","tagName":"md-inline-code","attributes":{},"children":[],"properties":{"html":"<span class=\"th-token th-function\">css</span>()","source":"css()"}},{"type":"text","value":" takes any number of arguments — objects, or handles you already made —\nand merges them left to right:"}]},{"type":"component","name":"code","tagName":"md-code","attributes":{},"children":[],"properties":{"source":"const base = css({ padding: \"0.5rem\" })\nconst wide = css(base, { paddingInline: \"1.5rem\" })","lang":"tsx","html":"<span class=\"th-token th-keyword\">const</span> base = <span class=\"th-token th-function\">css</span>({ <span class=\"th-token th-property\">padding</span>: <span class=\"th-token th-string\">&quot;0.5rem&quot;</span> })\n<span class=\"th-token th-keyword\">const</span> wide = <span class=\"th-token th-function\">css</span>(base, { <span class=\"th-token th-property\">paddingInline</span>: <span class=\"th-token th-string\">&quot;1.5rem&quot;</span> })"}},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Merging follows the "},{"type":"link","href":"/docs/styling/merging","children":[{"type":"text","value":"merge rules"}]},{"type":"text","value":": later entries replace\nmatching entries and leave the rest alone."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"shorthands","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Shorthands"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Shorthands are expanded to longhands, so two styles that touch the same box merge\nper side rather than wholesale:"}]},{"type":"component","name":"code","tagName":"md-code","attributes":{},"children":[],"properties":{"source":"const a = css({ padding: \"1rem\" })\nconst b = css({ paddingTop: \"2rem\" })\n\n<div sx={[a, b]} /> // 2rem on top, 1rem on the other three sides","lang":"tsx","html":"<span class=\"th-token th-keyword\">const</span> a = <span class=\"th-token th-function\">css</span>({ <span class=\"th-token th-property\">padding</span>: <span class=\"th-token th-string\">&quot;1rem&quot;</span> })\n<span class=\"th-token th-keyword\">const</span> b = <span class=\"th-token th-function\">css</span>({ <span class=\"th-token th-property\">paddingTop</span>: <span class=\"th-token th-string\">&quot;2rem&quot;</span> })\n\n&lt;<span class=\"th-token th-tag\">div</span> <span class=\"th-token th-attr\">sx</span>={[a, b]} /&gt; <span class=\"th-token th-comment\">// 2rem on top, 1rem on the other three sides</span>"}},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"A shorthand whose value cannot be split exactly — "},{"type":"inlineComponent","name":"inline-code","tagName":"md-inline-code","attributes":{},"children":[],"properties":{"html":"<span class=\"th-token th-property\">border</span>: <span class=\"th-token th-string\">&quot;var(--line)&quot;</span>","source":"border: \"var(--line)\""}},{"type":"text","value":", where\nthe value is one custom property — stays whole, and the compiler warns\n("},{"type":"inlineComponent","name":"inline-code","tagName":"md-inline-code","attributes":{},"children":[],"properties":{"html":"unsplittable-shorthand","source":"unsplittable-shorthand"}},{"type":"text","value":") because removing one of its longhands later cannot be\ndone precisely."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Mixing logical and physical longhands of the same box ("},{"type":"inlineComponent","name":"inline-code","tagName":"md-inline-code","attributes":{},"children":[],"properties":{"html":"paddingLeft","source":"paddingLeft"}},{"type":"text","value":" and\n"},{"type":"inlineComponent","name":"inline-code","tagName":"md-inline-code","attributes":{},"children":[],"properties":{"html":"paddingInlineStart","source":"paddingInlineStart"}},{"type":"text","value":") is allowed, but they are "},{"type":"emphasis","children":[{"type":"text","value":"different"}]},{"type":"text","value":" declarations, and when\nthe result could mislead the compiler says so ("},{"type":"inlineComponent","name":"inline-code","tagName":"md-inline-code","attributes":{},"children":[],"properties":{"html":"mixed-logical-physical","source":"mixed-logical-physical"}},{"type":"text","value":")."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"where-styles-live","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Where styles live"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"A handle is usually a module-level constant, because it compiles to a constant:"}]},{"type":"component","name":"code","tagName":"md-code","attributes":{},"children":[],"properties":{"source":"const styles = {\n  root: css({ … }),\n  title: css({ … }),\n}","lang":"tsx","html":"<span class=\"th-token th-keyword\">const</span> styles = {\n  <span class=\"th-token th-property\">root</span>: <span class=\"th-token th-function\">css</span>({ … }),\n  <span class=\"th-token th-property\">title</span>: <span class=\"th-token th-function\">css</span>({ … }),\n}"}},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Writing "},{"type":"inlineComponent","name":"inline-code","tagName":"md-inline-code","attributes":{},"children":[],"properties":{"html":"<span class=\"th-token th-function\">css</span>({ … })","source":"css({ … })"}},{"type":"text","value":" inside a component body is fine too — it still compiles —\nbut there is no reason to, unless the style depends on a value only known at\nrender time, which is its own topic:\n"},{"type":"link","href":"/docs/styling/dynamic","children":[{"type":"text","value":"dynamic values"}]},{"type":"text","value":"."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"next","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Next"}]},{"type":"list","ordered":false,"items":[{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"link","href":"/docs/styling/sx","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The "},{"type":"inlineComponent","name":"inline-code","tagName":"md-inline-code","attributes":{},"children":[],"properties":{"html":"sx","source":"sx"}},{"type":"text","value":" prop"}]},{"type":"text","value":" — putting a handle on an element."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"link","href":"/docs/styling/conditions","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Conditions"}]},{"type":"text","value":" — hover, breakpoints, attributes."}]}]}]}],"headings":[{"id":"writing-styles","text":"Writing styles","level":1},{"id":"property-names","text":"Property names","level":2},{"id":"values","text":"Values","level":2},{"id":"several-objects-one-handle","text":"Several objects, one handle","level":2},{"id":"shorthands","text":"Shorthands","level":2},{"id":"where-styles-live","text":"Where styles live","level":2},{"id":"next","text":"Next","level":2}]}
